1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,358
Excuse me. Is this seat taken?

2
00:00:04,358 --> 00:00:05,956
No, it's not taken.

3
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:09,434
Oh, thank you.

4
00:00:09,434 --> 00:00:16,390
Oh, let me help you with this.

5
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:17,223
Oh, thank you.

6
00:00:17,223 --> 00:00:19,439
Do you want to sit by the window?

7
00:00:19,439 --> 00:00:28,802
No, no, no. I like the aisle seat better.

8
00:00:28,802 --> 00:00:31,727
Please, you sit by the window.

9
00:00:31,727 --> 00:00:40,834
My name is Stewart... Malcolm Stewart.

10
00:00:40,834 --> 00:00:41,978
Pleased to meet you.

11
00:00:41,978 --> 00:00:44,025
I'm Elsa Tobin. How do you do?

12
00:00:44,025 --> 00:00:45,419
Do you live in New York?

13
00:00:45,419 --> 00:00:48,303
No, no. I'm from Florida.

14
00:00:48,303 --> 00:00:51,235
I am, too. But didn't you just get on?

15
00:00:51,235 --> 00:00:53,603
No, no. I just changed my seat.

16
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:59,906
A man next to me was smoking,

17
00:00:59,906 --> 00:01:01,639
and smoke really bothers me.

18
00:01:01,639 --> 00:01:04,470
Where are you from in Florida?

19
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:06,182
Titusville. It's near Orlando.

20
00:01:06,182 --> 00:01:10,493
Small world. I'm from Titusville, too.

21
00:01:10,493 --> 00:01:11,993
Really? What part?

22
00:01:11,993 --> 00:01:18,735
My husband and I live near Spaceport.

23
00:01:18,735 --> 00:01:35,878
I know that area.

24
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:36,078
My house is only a few miles from Spaceport.

25
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:36,078
Do you still live there?

26
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:36,078
Oh yes, yes. My husband's there now.

27
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:36,078
He couldn't take time off to come to New York with me.

28
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:36,078
Do you still live there?

29
00:01:35,878 --> 00:01:38,273
No. I sold the house and the furniture,

30
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:42,451
put a few personal things in an old trunk,

31
00:01:42,451 --> 00:01:45,729
and shipped it to my children in New York.

32
00:01:45,729 --> 00:01:47,207
That's my destination.

33
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:49,207
Are you married?

34
00:01:49,207 --> 00:01:51,518
My wife died four years ago.

35
00:01:51,518 --> 00:01:59,118
She was a wonderful woman. A real friend.

36
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:03,296
I'm sorry. Really, I'm sorry.

37
00:02:03,296 --> 00:02:06,021
Lots of wonderful memories.

38
00:02:06,021 --> 00:02:09,156
We were married almost fifty years.

39
00:02:09,156 --> 00:02:12,316
Well, forty-seven, to be exact.

40
00:02:12,316 --> 00:02:17,406
John and I celebrate our fortieth anniversary next month.

41
00:02:17,406 --> 00:02:21,059
Oh, congratulations! That's nice.

42
00:02:21,059 --> 00:02:22,519
What does John do?

43
00:02:22,519 --> 00:02:25,068
He's an aerospace engineer

44
00:02:25,068 --> 00:02:27,300
and works for Orlando Aircraft Corporation.

45
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:32,876
He started with them almost forty years ago.

46
00:02:32,876 --> 00:02:37,832
What do you do?

47
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:41,310
I just retired. Had my own company.

48
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:47,041
A construction company. Roads, bridges, big stuff.

49
00:02:47,041 --> 00:02:53,229
But I just sold it and retired.

50
00:02:53,229 --> 00:02:58,678
Excuse me, ma'am. Ticket, please.

51
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,656
Would you kindly hold these keys, please?

52
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:04,634
I have a ticket, I know.

53
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:07,612
I was in the smoking section.

54
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:11,669
It's OK, lady. Take your time.

55
00:03:11,669 --> 00:03:16,545
I'm sure it's in your purse, Mrs.Tobin.

56
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:20,663
Oh, here it is.

57
00:03:20,663 --> 00:03:26,479
And here are your keys.

58
00:03:26,479 --> 00:03:27,479
Thank you.

59
00:03:27,479 --> 00:03:31,790
Do you have family in New York?

60
00:03:31,790 --> 00:03:35,093
No, no. But I do have very close friends in New York City.

61
00:03:35,093 --> 00:03:38,141
We like to go to the theater together.

62
00:03:38,141 --> 00:03:43,753
You said you have family in New York.

63
00:03:43,753 --> 00:03:44,564
Yes, indeed.

64
00:03:44,564 --> 00:03:49,075
A son and his wife and their three children-

65
00:03:49,075 --> 00:03:49,714
my grandchildren.

66
00:03:49,714 --> 00:03:51,360
You must be excited.

67
00:03:51,360 --> 00:03:53,618
I can't wait, to see them!

68
00:03:53,618 --> 00:04:00,537
Are you going to live with them?

69
00:04:00,537 --> 00:04:01,687
Yes.

70
00:04:01,687 --> 00:04:01,887
Permanently?

71
00:04:01,687 --> 00:04:04,215
Well... they want me to,

72
00:04:04,215 --> 00:04:07,829
but it's too early to know for sure.

73
00:04:07,829 --> 00:04:08,815
I'm pretty independent.

74
00:04:08,815 --> 00:04:13,554
I tried to teach my kids the importance of independence,

75
00:04:13,554 --> 00:04:18,105
but I'm not sure I want to be alone.

76
00:04:18,105 --> 00:04:25,788
Some people don't mind being alone. I do.

77
00:04:25,788 --> 00:04:27,663
I understand. But tell me.

78
00:04:27,663 --> 00:04:33,972
Why did you stop working?

79
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:38,870
I retired because... I wanted to be with my family.

80
00:04:38,870 --> 00:04:41,870
I didn't want to be alone anymore!
